# Caddy config for the VPS edge (PLAN.md §7A/§7D, docs/vps-edge-deployment.md).
# Terminates public HTTPS (automatic Let's Encrypt) for one or more
# independent clusters' admin/api/portal subdomains and reverse-proxies
# admin/api to each cluster's own folia-nexa-mgmt, over that cluster's own
# WireGuard tunnel peer (deploy/vps/setup-wireguard.sh's multi-peer mesh).
# Minecraft traffic itself (:25565) is raw TCP, not HTTP — it never goes
# through Caddy; the relocated folia-nexa-proxy binds that port directly
# on the VPS and does its own per-cluster hostname routing (PLAN.md §7D,
# FoliaRoutesSyncPlugin/VirtualHostRouter). Same story for Bedrock
# (:19132/udp, RakNet, PLAN.md §7B) — also raw, also bound directly by
# folia-nexa-proxy, Caddy has no role in it either, and RakNet has no
# hostname/SNI concept so Bedrock can't be routed per-cluster regardless
# (see docs/vps-edge-deployment.md).
#
# Each cluster's admin/api/portal site blocks live in their own file
# under clusters.d/, generated by ./add-cluster.sh rather than hand-edited
# here — see clusters.d/README.md. A fresh checkout has zero clusters
# configured; run add-cluster.sh at least once before `caddy run`/reload,
# or the `import` below simply has nothing to import (an empty edge,
# not an error).
{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL:you@example.com}
}

import clusters.d/*.caddy
